# Node ESM harness scripts (apps/api/scripts, tools/) must check out with
# LF line endings on every platform. Git's core.autocrlf=true (the Windows
# default here) rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, and vitest 4 / Vite 8's
# SSR transform throws "Invalid or unexpected token" when it imports a CRLF
# `.mjs` (found the hard way: a stash/pop turned apps/api/scripts/lib/
# soakEvidence.mjs into CRLF and broke its test suite with no parse error
# under node/esbuild/rolldown — only the vitest pipeline choked).
*.mjs text eol=lf
